5332 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This discussion guide outlines the structure and flow of our upcoming research sessions\054 ensuring each conversation is consistent\054 purposeful\054 and aligned with the project\031s objectives\056 It provides a clear framework for how we will introduce the session\054 explore key themes\054 and close with reflections\054 while still allowing space for natural dialogue and participant\021led insights\056 The guide is not a script\054 but a flexible roadmap that helps us gather rich\054 comparable feedback in a way that feels comfortable and intuitive for participants\056\n\nResearch objectives\072\nValidate the hypothesis that users blocker to taking action is not seeing patterns in their thinking \nUnderstanding user  pain points with their current coping mechanisms and tools \nDay one value\nTo identify the condition or emotional trigger that would create an immediate value for a new user on day 1\056 \nPrivacy\nTo uncover users privacy concerns and what makes them feel safe enough to integrate their private notes\057reflections to Spark \nHabit formation\nTo uncover what would motivate habitual return visits to an app\057platform over others\n\nContext\072\n\nThe Spark project addresses a\240deeply human challenge\072 helping individuals break free from inherited mental scripts and rediscover authentic meaning and purpose\056 We have been assigned by the client to design a solution that will help users take small steps towards what matters and help people reconnect with their own wisdom\nI\031m not looking for perfect answer\054 just honest experiences\056 Feel free to take your time\056 There\031s no expectation to have things figured out\056 I\031m much more interested in the messy\054 real parts\056 if something doesn\031t resonate\054 we can move on\056 I really appreciate you being open with me\056\n\nBackground questions \nWhat does a typical day look like for you at the moment\077 \nWhat is currently taking up most of your mental space\077 \nWhen you feel mentally cluttered or overwhelmed\054 what do you usually do to make sense of things\077 \n\nCurrent coping mechanisms \046 pain points \nDo you currently stop and take time to reflect\077 what does this look like for you\077 \nWalk me through your process of capturing an idea or reflection that resonates with you\056 Where does it go and what happen usually to it a week or so later\077\nHave you ever noticed patterns in your thinking or behaviour\077 How did you recognise them\077\nWhich apps or tools have you tried for notes\054 journaling or reflection \057 for each\054 what was great\077 what made you stop or feel overwhelmed\077 \nTell me about a time you felt overwhelmed by the amount of information you\031ve collected \050saved notes\054 articles\054 podcast\056\056books\051 how did you handle that feeling of mental clutter\077 \n\nMoments of meaning and connection \046 action\nCan you think of the last time you felt really aligned to yourself\054 what supported you in that moment\077 \nWhen you know or almost what you want to do what gets in the way of taking the first step\077\n\nPrivacy\nHow do you usually decide whether to grant an app permission to access your private data\054 like notes and reflections\077  What makes digital tool feel like a safe\077 \nWhat are you afraid to share\077 what data feels most personal to you and why\077 \n\nDay 1 value\072\nThink back to the last time you downloaded or used a new tool for your personnel notes or growth\054 within those first few minutes\054 what was that small discovery or quick win that made decide it was worth keeping\077\n\nHabits and notifications\nWhat\031s the difference between a notification being annoying vs helpful\077 \nWhen you know or almost what you want to do what gets in the way of taking the first step\077\nIf an app could surface an insight from your past thoughts at exactly the right moment\054 what would you want that moment to feel like\077\n\nThe core metaphor Star \046 Constellations \n\nSpark uses a metaphor of \047Stars and Constellations\047 to describe your thoughts\054 notes and reflections\056 What does this mean to you\077 And what image do you see\077\n\nClose and final question\nIs there anything else you would like to share\077 \n\nInterest in usability testing\nWould you be interested in participating in some usability testing\077 \nIt\031s happening on X day\054 can we book in a time\077 \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n)
     /K [ 194 ]
     /P 5333 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

