5517 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Kim loves spotting patterns in thinking\054 she does this consciously through daily and weekly reflection times\054 but also by actively interrogating feelings of discomfort when they show up\056 Spotting patterns aren\031t just interesting to her\054 it\031s a way to build self\055trust and clarity\056 \n\nShe is an experienced coach\054 and already has an external system that stores her thoughts\054 ideas\054 and reflections\056 She has mature ways of getting herself to action\054 by breaking things down\054 externalising the steps\054 using environmental cues\056 She knows motivation follows action and coaches others through this transition\056 In moments of connecting patterns\054 she talked about it feeling more intuitive\054 or something larger at play \055  \030 is the world is trying to tell me something\077\031\056 \n\nShe believes the key to moving into action is seizing the spark\054 capturing it\054 so that it turns into action\056 Even something as small as writing the thing down so you can see it\054 or putting it on an email\056\n\nKnowledge is strongly linked to self trust for her\056 But the tension is she wants a coherent view of her experience\054 but she doesn\031t want to be reduced \050i\056e\056 neurodiversity diagnosis\051\056 She is still curious about understanding how her brain works\054 and her patterns in responses so that she can feel more in control without loosing a sense of relaxations and comfort with spontaneity\056\n\nThe opportunity for Spark is to help her understand herself and spot patterns quickly in a way that doesn\031t feel reductive\056 \n\n\n)
     /K [ 287 ]
     /P 5518 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

5518 0 obj
  << /K [ 5517 0 R ]
     /P 10187 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

