6959 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Notes from KO meeting \nKO meeting\nFri\054 20 Mar 26\nTeam Introductions and Project Context\nLucy\072 Research and strategy background\054 project management lead focusing on ideation and information architecture\nSarah\072 Ex\055graphic designer\057marketer transitioning to UX\054 leading synthesis\054 interviews\054 ideation and prototyping\naKosua\072 10\053 years social work experience\054 leading data synthesis\054 interviews and prototyping\nSavio\072 Communication strategy advisor and mentor from Brazil\054 identifies blind spots for Nirish\054 will participate in key collaborative sessions\n\nProblem Definition and Vision\nPlatform for people conditioned to follow prescribed life scripts \050school \222 job \222 corporate ladder \222 retirement\051\nTarget users questioning these pathways\054 especially in tech industry facing layoffs and AI job displacement\nCore issue\072 People lose identity and meaning when jobs disappear\054 lack self\055awareness of who they are beyond external validation\nLong\055term vision\072 Pioneer \034meaning tech\035 category \055 technology helping humans find purpose and self\055actualization\nComparison to fintech\054 edtech\054 healthtech but focused on fundamental human need for meaning\nParticularly relevant as AI\057UBI may eliminate traditional job\055based meaning\n\nThe Spark Concept and User Journey\nThree\055part cycle\072 Self\055awareness \222 Creative courage \222 Meaning discovery\nUsers mind dump thoughts\057feelings into app during moments of doubt\054 boredom\054 or misalignment\nAI analyzes personal knowledge repository \050notes\054 saves\054 bookmarks\051 to surface forgotten insights\nProvides \034sparks\035 \055 connections between current situation and past learnings\nOffers time\055based micro\055actions \0502\054 5\054 or 15 minutes\051 to build self\055trust through small experiments\nIncludes reflection and celebration phases to reinforce positive behavior loops\n\nCurrent Prototype Walkthrough\nBasic demo with mind dump functionality and timer elements designed to encourage engagement\nSpark generation currently uses dummy data due to broken database connections\nShows source attribution to build user trust in AI recommendations\nIncorporates calming elements \050similar to Headspace\051 into user flow\nFocus on reducing barriers to action and embracing discomfort of trying new things\nVictory celebration features to help users acknowledge small wins\n\nKey Design Challenges Identified\nDay one value\072 How to provide immediate benefit for users without existing data repository\nBiggest unknown challenge that may require alternative onboarding approaches\nOpen to quiz\057survey mechanisms or structured first\055week data collection\nTrust building\072 Getting users to connect personal data sources to AI system\nHabit formation\072 Breaking doom\055scrolling patterns\054 redirecting to \034social media of your own mind\035\nNotification strategy\072 Timely delivery of relevant insights\nEach challenge represents sequential customer lifecycle stage\n\nResearch Approach and Participant Overview\n8 participants scheduled across Monday\055Wednesday\nMix includes GA instructors\054 product designers\054 coaches\054 researchers\nNotable participants\072\nKate \050Monday 11am\051\072 GA instructor\057manager\054 lacks confidence as strengths coach\054 overthinker\nSavio \050Monday 1\07215pm\051\072 Subject matter expert interview rather than user interview\nEgla \050Tuesday 11\07245am\051\072 Classic ICP\054 highly successful corporate background wanting independence\nLucia \050Wednesday 10\07215am\051\072 Senior UX researcher with large Evernote database\054 fears AI integration\nTeam will focus first round on problem validation before usability testing\n\nTechnical Considerations and Future Features\nNo current technical constraints given rapid technology advancement\nPotential social media integration to map interests and passions\072\nInstagram saves\057likes\054 YouTube history\054 LinkedIn engagement\nCreate personalized interest map for more intentional forward steps\nVoice banking technology consideration using tools like Descript \05030\055minute voice sample\051\nCommunity features allowing collaborative knowledge sharing between users\nZebra startup model rather than unicorn approach\072 )
     /K [ 1008 ]
     /P 6963 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
