  << /ActualText (Simon \055 Head of product at MYOB\n\nWho he is\nAction\055oriented\054 operational thinker\056 Busy with family\054 does a lot of writing\054 creative projects\054 and \042life admin\056\n\nCore problem \nSimon suggests that seeing patterns is the easier part\056 The harder part is being honest enough with himself to act on what they reveal\056 The blocker are willingness\054 consistency\054 readiness and physical fatigue\056 \n\nPattern awareness\nSimon can see patterns\054 he circles recurring words\054 uses backlinking\056\n\nNotes and reflection practice and paint point\nUses Obsidian \050recently migrated from Logseq\051\056\nHandwrite on Moleskine journal as he like the free\055flow thinking and writing\056\nHas a personal \042Attention \222 Intention \222 Action\042 morning framework\nJournaling is inconsistent busyness and tiredness kill the habit\n\nThe reasons he reflects\nBelieves unexamined emotions keep resurfacing until acknowledged\054\n\nHabit formation\nHis best habit \050morning practice\051 works because it\047s values\055anchored \024 Attention \222 Intention \222 Action is his framework\054 developed by him\054 for him\056 He trusts it because he built it\056\n\nDay one value\nQuality of first AI response\054 direct\054 pragmatic\054 no flattery\056 He used the word \042sycophantic\042 twice as an instant turn\055off\nSpeed and frictionlessness\054 keyboard shortcuts\054 fast organisation\054 bold\057links\057folders\056 If it slows him down\054 it\047s dead\056\nFeels like it belongs to him\054 the tool should reflect his input back to him\054 not pull him into someone else\047s content or agenda\056\n\nPrivacy\nAny suggestion his notes train a model would end the relationship immediately\056What would make him feel safe\072 Explicit data ownership\054 no proprietary lock\055in\054 transparent and limited use of his data\054 local\055first or exportable architecture\056\n\nOpportunity for Spark\n\n\n\n\n)
