8220 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Konstantinos \055 \n\nWho he is\nGreek designer from Evia\054 living in London\056 Left full\055time role to slow down\054 rediscover values\054 and figure out what meaningful work looks like for him\056 Design is a lifestyle\054 not a job\056\n\nCore problem\nHis actual blockers were\072\nRunning out of momentum after the insight phase \050\042I\047d run out of gas\042\051\nLacking technical ability to build what he envisioned \050Faces of Greece sat dormant for years\051\nBeing inside a system that actively suppressed his values\n\nPattern awareness\nHe could see his patterns eventually through journaling\056 \n\nNotes and reflection practice and paint point\nKonstantinos has a functioning second brain \050Notion\051\054 an AI query layer \050Claude\051\054 a journaling practice\054 and pattern\055recognition habits\056 He got there through years of iteration\054 external coaching\n\nThe reasons he reflects\n\nDay one value\nHe doesn\047t want to be impressed by capability\056 He wants the tool to demonstrate it already understands something about him\056 The Positive Intelligence reference is telling\056 what he loved was that it learned him without forcing him\056 His ideal onboarding is a tool that asks the right questions\054 not one that shows off its feature set\056 The emotional job here is\072 \042This tool sees me\056\042\n\nPrivacy\nHis privacy framework is strikingly rational\072 paid service \075 fair exchange\054 free service \075 exploitation\056 He\047s not anxious about sharing data\056\nHe wants to know\072 what are you taking\054 what am I getting\054 are you training other models on it\077\n\nHabit formation\n\nNotification\nHe doesn\047t just dislike notifications\073 he\047s already diagnosed why they fail and asked the right design question\072 \042How do you notify someone without notifying them\077\042 The Japan bird\055sound provocation wasn\047t idle creativity\054 it was a genuine design principle\072 ambient\054 contextual\054 non\055demanding signals that serve the user without interrupting them\056 This is a sophisticated ask that most notification systems completely ignore\056\n\nOpportunity and implications  for Spark\n\n\n\n\n)
