8224 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Kim\055  Consultant and Professional Coach \n\nWho she is\nDeeply reflective\054 pattern\055oriented thinker who enjoys processing information\n Experienced coach with strong self\055awareness and established personal systems\nCurious about understanding how her mind works\054 without wanting to be reduced or labelled\n\nCore problem\nTension between gaining clarity and not wanting her identity or thinking to feel reductive\n\nPattern awareness\nActively spots patterns through reflection and by interrogating moments of discomfort\n Recognises themes across situations\054 but these often emerge after the fact rather than in the moment\n\nNotes and reflection practice and paint point\nUses multiple systems \050Notion\054 email\054 bookmarking\054 tags\051 to capture and organise information\nPain point\072 system is complex and fragmented\054 making it harder to easily connect and surface patterns\n\nThe reasons she reflects\nTrying to empty her mind from all her thoughts and the complexity of the world and demands on her attention \n\nDay one value\nA simple\054 intuitive way to connect and make sense of information quickly\nFeeling that insights are easy to access and not buried in complex systems\n\nPrivacy\nMore cautious and selective\073 wary of large systems and unclear data use\n More comfortable sharing when there is a clear purpose and a sense of trust or human intention \050like research\051 \n\nHabit formation\nStrong ability to move into action by breaking things down into small steps\nUses environmental cues and externalisation\073 believes action creates motivation\n\nOpportunity and implications for Spark\nHelp Kim see and understand patterns in her thinking quickly and clearly\054 without adding complexity\nProvide insight in a way that builds self\055understanding without feeling reductive or overly defined\n\n\n\n\n\n)
