8236 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Egle\n\nWho she is\nCommunication strategist \057 coach based in Germany\056 This could be an SME \050Subject Matter Expert\051 interview to uncover best practices and challenges he\047s seen in the industry related to managing one\047s own knowledge\054 connecting the dots and creating meaningful value out into the world\056\n\nCore problem\072\ncore struggle is fragmentation\024her ideas\054 reflections\054 and creative sparks are scattered across multiple tools\054 devices\054 and formats\056 This fragmentation prevents her from seeing patterns\054 building momentum\054 and acting on long\021held aspirations\056 She knows she has valuable ideas\054 but without a system that connects them\054 they stagnate\056 The emotional layer is equally important\072 fear\054 self\021doubt\054 and overthinking often block her from taking action\054 especially on meaningful personal projects\056\n\nPattern awareness\072\nShe is highly self\021aware and recognizes several recurring patterns\072\nShe overthinks and often needs someone else to confirm whether she\031s spiralling or being reasonable\056\nShe processes ideas through conversation\024others provide \03450\045 of her creative momentum\056\035\nCreativity behaves like a muscle for her\073 without regular practice\054 it weakens\056\nShe maintains a mental map of where ideas live\054 even in chaos\054 but knows this is unsustainable\056\nShe avoids forcing ideas\073 they need time to digest before being captured\056\nThis awareness makes her open to tools that help her see herself more clearly\024but only if they respect her autonomy and privacy\056\n\nNotes and reflection practice and paint point\072\nuses a patchwork of tools\072 Mac Notes\054 Google Keep\054 physical notebooks\054 voice recordings\054 and planners\056 Each serves a purpose\054 but none work together\056 Google Keep becomes a \034cemetery\035 of forgotten notes\056 Mac Notes requires heavy manual categorization\056 Planners never fit and must be customized\056 She captures ideas easily but struggles to revisit\054 connect\054 or develop them\056 Reflection happens naturally\024during walks\054 quiet mornings\054 or conversations\024but her tools don\031t support the fluidity of her thinking\056\nThe pain point isn\031t capturing ideas\073 it\031s making sense of them later\056\n\nThe reasons she reflects\nUnderstand herself and her patterns\nStrengthen her creative muscle\nMake sense of emotional states\nMove long\021held ideas toward action\nAvoid stagnation after years of corporate intensity\nReconnect with her identity beyond productivity\nReflection is both a grounding practice and a creative engine\056\n\nDay one value\072\nA tool earns a second chance if it delivers\072\nImmediate clarity \024 no clutter\054 no cognitive load\nA sense of possibility \024 it helps her see something she couldn\031t see alone\nA quick win \024 capturing something effortlessly or surfacing a meaningful connection\nFlexibility \024 it adapts to her\054 not the other way around\nRigid templates or overwhelming interfaces are abandoned instantly\056\n\nPrivacy\072 \nPrivacy is non\021negotiable\056 After past data breaches\054 she revoked Claude\031s learning permissions\054 stopped using ChatGPT\054 and avoids tools that store or analyze data in the cloud\056 She wants\072\nLocal\021only storage\nExplicit control over what is shared\nNo algorithmic training\nTransparency about data handling\nHer ideas feel deeply personal\024almost like an extension of her identity\024so trust must be earned\054 not assumed\056\n\nHabit formation\072\nHer habits are shaped by energy\054 not discipline\056 She works in cycles\072\nHigh\021clarity mornings\nLow\021energy afternoons requiring movement\nReflection during walks\nCreative bursts when emotionally grounded\nShe doesn\031t force creativity\073 she creates conditions for it\056 Notifications must be rare\054 relevant\054 and well\021timed\024otherwise she disengages immediately\056\n\nOpportunity for Spark\n\nSpark has a powerful opening with Egle  by becoming the central\054 private\054 cross\021platform home for her ideas\054 one that\072\nAccepts all input types \050typing\054 handwriting\054 sketching\054 voice\054 transcription\051\nAutomatically finds patterns across her scattered notes\nHelps her connect ideas into meaningful constellations\nSurfaces insights at the right moment\nSupports her emotional and creative journey\054 not just her productivity\nEncourages courageous action through gentle prompts and reflective questions\nRespects her privacy with local\021first architecture and explicit user control\nMost importantly\054 Spark can help her do what no tool currently does\072 turn her reflections into momentum\054 bridging the gap between insight and action while honouring her need for safety\054 flexibility\054 and human\021centred support\n\n\n\n\n)
