  << /ActualText (Stage 5\072 Taking the \042Small Act of Courage\042\n\nThe user breaks down their overwhelming goal into a tiny\054 manageable task to build evidence of self\055trust\056\nGoals\072 Build momentum\073 \042seize the spark\042 before it extinguishes\056\nPains\072 High friction to starting\073 perfectionism\056\nNeeds\072 \042Stupidly clear\042 first steps\073 micro\055actions that take only 2\05515 minutes\056\nCurrent Workarounds\072 Posting a single tweet instead of a full blog\073 just \042lying on a yoga mat\042 for 30 seconds\056\nQuotes\072\n\042I\047m just trying to maybe explore the smallest tiny bit I can do for now\056\056\056 it makes me feel a bit better\056\042 \024 Lin Q\n\042Make the first step stupidly clear\056\056\056 it should feel stupid as you write it down\056\042 \024 Kim W)
