8929 0 obj
  << /ActualText (It\031s getting towards the end of busy week at work and Lauren is at home on the couch with a cup of coffee\056 Friday morning is the day she usually sits down for her end of week reflections\056 She knows she\031s had a good week\054 lots of thought\055provoking conversations with lots of interesting people\054 but she can\031t quite make sense of what they mean\054 and is unsure of what to do next\056 She\031s been capturing her ideas and reflections throughout the week\054 albeit in a bit of a scattered approach \055 personal reflections in her hand\055written journal\054 ideas for her podcast and from conversations she\031s had whilst on the go in her iPhone notes and Obsidian when she\031s remembered to\056 \n\nShe\031d usually go through everything manually\054 circling repeated words and capturing key points to take forward and action into the next week\056 But today\054 the manual synthesis feels so effortful\056 Trying to do something out of the ordinary\054 break away from the 9\0555 routine is hard enough as it is\056 She\031s feeling tired\054 doubting herself\056 She really wants to keep moving ahead with launching her podcast\054 but the idea of putting herself out there is so daunting\056 What if no\055body likes it\077 Feeling defeated\054 the easier feels like opening instagram and have a scroll\056 \n\nBut\054 she remembers one of her coaching friends mentioning a new tool\054 Spark\056 It\031s meant to help spot patterns in ideas\054 thoughts\054 reflections and guide you towards small courageous steps\056\n\nShe opens the tool\056 It asks her to share a bit about what she\031s struggling with today and what she wants to get done\056 Putting the thoughts down is already helping her get some clarity\056 Things are starting to feel a bit less scary\056 She writes that she is feeling stuck\054 overwhelmed\054 but wants to do something towards launching her podcast over the weekend\054 maybe write a blog post\056 She\031s feeling so defeated today and wants some advice on how to carry the excitement of the conversations she\031s had this week into action\056 \n\nSpark asks her if she\031d be willing to upload any of her notes from the week\077 This feels quite personal\054 but she\031s happy to\056 Spark seems like a small organisations that she can trust\056 Unlike those big tech corporates\056 She\031s happy to see that they are being transparent about what happens to her data\054 and has the option to control privacy settings\056 She feels comfortable sharing with the app now\056 She takes some photos of her journals\054 and screenshots from her notes from the week and uploads it to Spark\056 Just sharing this with something else has made her feel lighter\056 \n\nAlmost instantly it comes back to her\056\056\056 it\031s spotted a pattern\056 A theme from her conversations that could be worth exploring in her podcast blog \030resilience\031\056 And it\031s summarised a few of her feelings from her journal entries \055 fear is a key theme\056 Just seeing this helps her to feel more accepting of the feeling\054 it creates some distance between her and the fear\056 \n\nShe realises this is a familiar feeling \055 she felt the exact same last time she had to speak on a panel at a conference\056 She shares these reflections back with Spark\056 She\031s feeling much clearer and less cluttered mentally\056  Spark asks her if she wants to create an action plan to help her with this challenge\077 Yes please\041 It comes back with 5 simple steps to action over the next week\056 \030That doesn\031t seem so hard\031 she thinks\056\056\056 but how am I going to keep myself accountable\077 She usually relies on deadlines\054 and meetings with people to keep on track\056 She edits the steps\054 adding dates and personalising it\056 \n\nStep 1 \055 Saturday\072 quickly write down 3 thoughts you\031ve had about resilience this week \nStep 2 \055Monday\072 tweet about resilience \nStep 3 \055 Tuesday\072 create an outline for your blog post \nStep 4 \055 Wednesday\072 share it with someone for feedback\nStep 5  \055 Friday\072 Post it to your network and celebrate\041 \n\nLauren confirms this plan\041 \055 Spark celebrates\041 \n\nit\031s suddenly feeling very real\056 Step 5 feels so far away\041 What does that even look like she wonders\077 Spark shows her a short animation of her completing all these tasks\054 some uplifting music plays and she is guided through imagining herself successfully reaching step 5\056 Okay\054 step 1 is very manageable\041 She thinks\056 I\031ll do this now\041\n\nShe writes down the 3 things\054 her energy is already returning\056 She ticks off the step\056 Spark congratulates her\054 and reminds her to take some time for herself today\056 Taking action isn\031t easy\054 but she\031s done it\041 \n\nShe relaxes and spends time switching off on the weekend\056 Monday comes around\054 and Spark gives her a nudge to remind her that Step 2 is due today\056 A tweet\056\056 oh that sounds fun\054 she thinks\041 \n\n)
     /K [ 1996 ]
     /P 8930 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
