  << /ActualText (Setting\nIt\047s a weekday evening\056 Lauren is on the tube home from the office\054 standing in the aisle\054 phone out but not really taking anything in\056 The day ran long and produced little\056 In the background\054 as always at this hour\054 is the podcast idea\056 The one she keeps moving to tomorrow\056\nShe steps off the train into the cold\056 That in\055between moment not at work\054 not yet home\056 A friend\047s message arrives on the walk\056 Just a link and a line\072 this reminded me of you\056\nShe opens it\056 Still walking\056 Still not quite ready to be done with the day\056\n\nThe narrative\nThe landing page doesn\047t promise to organise her life\056 It says something closer to\072 your thinking is already in there let\047s find it\056 That framing is different enough that she keeps reading\056\nShe signs up without overthinking it\056\nThen the app asks her something she didn\047t expect\056 Not connect your notes or set your goals\056 Just\072 what\047s on your mind right now\077\nShe types without thinking too hard\072 I want to start a podcast but I keep putting it off and I don\047t know if the idea is good enough\056\nSpark doesn\047t respond with advice\056 It asks if she wants to connect one place where she already keeps notes\056 Not all of them\056 Just one\054 to start\056\nShe connects Apple Notes\056 The one she actually uses\054 even if it\047s messy\056\nSpark surfaces something she wrote weeks ago barely two sentences\054 a passing thought about being afraid to share her voice publicly\056 Beneath it\054 two other notes where the same fear appeared without her realising\056 She reads them\056 There is a moment of quiet recognition\056 She has been circling this for months without naming it\056 It was there the whole time\054 buried in her own words\056\nSpark doesn\047t tell her what to do\056 It asks\072 does this feel true\077\nShe taps yes\056\nIt offers her one next step\056 Not the podcast\056 Not the episode plan\056 Just\072 write one sentence about what you want people to feel when they listen\056 Small enough to do right now\054 standing in her kitchen waiting for the kettle\056\nShe does it\056\nShe closes the app feeling lighter not because she solved anything\054 but because something that lived as background noise now has a shape\056)
