8939 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Key steps\nStep 1 Discovery\072 A trusted friend sends the link\056 Not an ad\054 not an algorithm\056 Someone who knows her thought it was worth her time\056 That is the permission she needed to open it\056\nStep 2 First input before setup\072 Instead of asking Lauren to build a system\054 Spark asks what is on her mind right now\056 She has something to do immediately\054 before the product has any of her data\056 This is what keeps her from closing the app\056\nStep 3 One source\054 not all of them\072 Spark asks her to connect a single note source\056 The ask is small enough that she doesn\047t have time to talk herself out of it\056 The fragmented system she has been ashamed of becomes the starting point\054 not a problem to fix first\056\nStep 4 The first insight\072 One pattern\056 One note shown back to her in a new light\056 Not a dashboard\054 not a summary  something specific and personal that she recognises immediately as true\056 This moment is the entire product compressed into a single screen\056 It either lands or it doesn\047t\056\nStep 5  Confirmation and agency\072 Spark asks does this feel true\077 Lauren decides\056 The insight only moves forward if she says yes\056 This is what separates Spark from every other tool she has tried it reflects\054 it doesn\047t prescribe\056\nStep 6 The micro\055action\072 The smallest possible next step\054 built from her own words\056 Not the overwhelming goal she has been avoiding the first stone across the river\056 She can edit it\056 She chooses it\056 It takes less energy to do it than to keep carrying it\056\nStep 7 Quiet closure\072 She completes the action\056 Spark acknowledges it simply\056 No streak\054 no score\054 no confetti\056 Just the felt sense of having moved\054 which is the reward Lauren actually needs\056)
