9443 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Annotation\n\nPurpose of the screen\072 \nIntroduces Spark\031s core value proposition using short embedded video\nRemove the cognitive clutter of reading a wall of text\054 user will be able to watch the product come to life in under 60sc\nThe user can see the end results before committing to anything \050the constellation\054 the small step taken\051\n\nUI elements\072 \nHeadline\072 \042In a few minutes\054 upload your notes\054 discover new patterns\054 and take small steps forward\042\nEmbedded video player\054 no fullscreen\056 Tap to play \057 pause\056 Thin coral progress bar at the bottom of the video \nBackground is a starry night sky same ambient field as the landing screen\054 stars continue twinkling\nThere is an audio toggle at the bottom and calming ambient music playing\nNo CTA button on this screen user taps the screen or swipes to advance\n\nInteractions\nThe user can toggle audio on and off\nThe user taps the screen to move on\nContinue after video finishes \n\nHow the user should feel\072 \nIntrigued\054 \034I want to see if I can do that for me\035\nReassured\054 \034This is not complicated\035\nCalm\054 \034the sound is so relaxing\035\n \n\n)
     /K [ 2254 ]
     /P 9444 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

9444 0 obj
  << /K [ 9443 0 R ]
     /P 10187 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

9445 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Annotation \n\nPurpose of the screen\072 \nTranslate the video into plain language three steps\054 clearly named\054 nothing technical\nGives the user a mental model they can hold before they are asked to do anything\072 upload \222 patterns \222 action\nBridges the gap between \042what is this\042 and \042I understand how to use this\042 \n \nUI elements\072 \nSection heading\072 \042How it works\042 in Playfair Display\nStep 1\072 Upload your notes any app\054 any format\nStep 2\072 Spark finds your patterns  connections you haven\047t seen yet\nStep 3\072 Take one small steps toward something that matters\nBackground is a starry night sky constellation lines begin to form faintly behind the three steps as a visual metaphor\nAudio toggle at the bottom remains visible\n\nInteractions\nStatic screen no input required\nThe user can toggle audio on and off\nThe user taps the screen to move on \n\nHow the user should feel\072 \nThe steps feel small not a system to learn\n)
     /K [ 2255 ]
     /P 9446 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

