9905 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Product Requirements Document\nUnthinking Space\240 \174\240 UX Design Sprint 2026\nVersion 1\0560\240 \174\240 March 2026\n\nA Meaning\055Tech application that helps users surface insights from fragmented knowledge and take small courageous steps toward a more meaningful life\056\n\n\n1\056 Product Overview\n\n1\0561 Product Vision\nSpark is a Meaning\055Tech application that helps people surface insights from their own fragmented knowledge\054 see patterns in their thinking\054 and take small courageous steps toward a more meaningful life\056\nIt is not a productivity tool\054 a meditation app\054 or a journaling diary\056 It sits at a new intersection\072 self\055awareness\054 knowledge management\054 and creative courage\056 \n\nHow spark is differentiated from other apps\072 \n\n1\0562 Brand Mantra\n\042I unthink\054 therefore I become\056\042\n\n1\0563 Strategic Positioning\nSpark\047s positioning differentiates it from every adjacent category\072\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2\056 The Problem space\n\nResearch across nine user interviews identified two distinct but connected core problems\056 These were validated in the client ideation workshop and agreed as the design priority\056\n\nProblem 1\072 Getting Over the Fear\nUsers want to act more fearlessly on the patterns they see because they trust these insights\054 but even when the pattern or clarity emerges they do not feel ready\054 because fear of failure and waiting for a good feeling keeps them in the thinking phase and delays action\056\n\nProblem 2\072 Understanding the patterns  \nUsers need the right insight delivered during the right moment because they lack the time and skill to manually connect the dots between their fragmented thoughts and notes\056\n\nResearch evidence\072\nIdeas are captured everywhere but never revisited notes\054 voice memos\054 screenshots\054 messages to themself\nNotes quickly become passive graveyards\072 they hold meaning in the moment but are never resurfaced\nManual synthesis is exhausting users want the connection made for them\054 not by them\nMemory is unreliable users cannot reconstruct what helped them during previous transitions\n\042I\047ve got three years of journal notes and I still can\047t tell you what helped me through my last career change\056 I have all this information but I still don\047t really know myself\056\042\n\nResearch evidence\072\nFear and self\055doubt are the primary blockers not lack of insight or information\nUsers wait for permission or external validation before acting on what they already know\nPerfectionism keeps users in the thinking phase they wait for the right moment that never comes\nWhen goals are broken into the smallest possible step\054 the emotional barrier to action drops significantly\n\042My notes become a cemetery  unorganised\054 unconnected\054 and impossible to act on\056\042\n\n\n\n)
     /K [ 2486 ]
     /P 9906 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

