10153 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Feature Requirements\n\nThe following features are derived directly from the research findings\054 the ideation workshop\054 and the wireframe review\056 They are organised by the three key flows identified in the brief\056\n\n6\0561 Flow One \024 Onboarding\n\nF1\0561 Opening question \024 first input before setup\nThe first screen Lauren sees after sign\055up must not ask her to connect notes\054 set goals\054 or configure anything\056 It must ask a single open question\072 what is on your mind right now\077 This anchors the session in her present state and gives her something to do before the product has any of her data\056\nSingle text input\054 no character limit\054 no formatting options\nVoice input option for users in motion\nNo required fields beyond this first input\n\nF1\0562 Single source connection\nSpark must ask Lauren to connect one note source\054 not all of them\056 The ask must be explicitly framed as a starting point\054 not a full import\056 Privacy language at this step must be warm\054 specific\054 and free of any legal or technical framing\056\nSupported integrations\072 Apple Notes\054 Google Keep\054 Notion\054 plain text \057 paste\nExplicit messaging\072 your notes stay yours \024 Spark reads them to find patterns\054 nothing is stored externally without your permission\nOption to paste directly if she does not want to connect a tool\n\nF1\0563 Day one value \nthe first spark\nThe first thing Spark returns must feel personally surprising\056 Not a category\054 not a summary \024 a specific moment from her own writing returned in a new light\056 This is the product\047s most critical moment and must be treated as such in the design\056\nSurface one pattern\054 not a dashboard\nShow the source note or notes that generated the pattern\nDisplay a short\054 specific narrative in the user\047s own language \024 not generic insight language\nFollow with\072 does this feel true\077 \024 with options to confirm or regenerate\n\n6\0562 Flow Two \024 First Time Use\n\nF2\0561 Constellation view \024 map of connections\nAfter the first insight is confirmed\054 Spark presents a visual map of connections \024 the constellation\056 This represents Lauren\047s patterns rendered as connected nodes\054 not a list or a grid\056 The metaphor of stars forming constellations should be felt\054 not explained\056\nVisual\054 not tabular \024 nodes connected by relationship strength\nShort narrative below the constellation\072 the story behind this pattern\nDoes this feel true\077 with two options\072 No \024 regenerate \057 Yes \024 take some small steps\nTapping a node reveals the source note\n\nF2\0562 The courage ladder\nWhen Lauren confirms an insight\054 Spark generates a courage ladder \024 a visual path of small steps from her current self toward the goal the pattern points to\056 The ladder is visual\054 not text\055based\056 Each rung is a stepping stone\054 not a task\056\nThree to five rungs generated from the confirmed insight\nEach rung has a short label visible on the ladder\nA figure or visual metaphor connecting current self to future self \050the star\051\nOption to visualise how it would feel to act out these steps before committing\n\nF2\0563 Editable steps\nLauren must be able to edit any rung on the ladder\056 The edit function must be visible and invited \024 not hidden in a menu\056 The act of editing a step is the act of owning it\056\nTap any rung to open the edit view\nEditable fields\072 step label\054 description\054 tone\nEdit and Add step options visible without needing a secondary menu\nChanges save automatically \024 no save button\n\nF2\0564 Editable roadmap inside each step\nEach rung on the ladder contains its own internal roadmap \024 a set of prompts and sub\055steps generated by Spark to help Lauren move through that step\056 She can edit this roadmap freely\056\nSub\055steps editable\072 label\054 content\054 order\nAdd sub\055step function available within each rung\nDelete individual sub\055steps without affecting the rung above\nRoadmap reshapes around changes without losing structural integrity\nHow does this feel to you\077 slider \024 Easy to Hard \024 adjusts Spark\047s suggestions for subsequent steps\n\nF2\0565 Completing a step\nWhen Lauren completes a step\054 Spark acknowledges it simply\056 No streak counter\054 no score\054 no gamification\056 The celebration is quiet and personal \024 a reminder that she moved\054 not that the app is pleased with her\056\nComplete button activates when step conditions are met or user self\055reports completion\nCompletion screen\072 congratulations moment with visual that connects to her journey\nReminder to celebrate \024 take some time for yourself today\nRoute back to the ladder showing the completed rung)
     /K [ 2610 ]
     /P 10154 0 R
     /Pg 4945 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

